Sval: the update elevation window says what it asks for

The window opens when the user can't write to the app bundle. It headed
itself Update Ready to Install, called every update a security and
stability update, and spent four sentences on administrator privileges
and the choices its buttons already name. It says an administrator must
approve the update and when macOS asks for the password.

diff --git a/toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/updates/elevation.ftl b/toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/updates/elevation.ftl
